corator returns the original callable, so srv.search_matches is callable directly. But careful: my module-level tools — `@mcp.tool()` decorated functions become plain functions still callable. Yes signature says returns the same callable. Update tests to call directly.\n- Cop a do Brasil ≥1300: file has 1337, fine.\n- players tests: club \"Santos\", name \"Gabriel Jesus\", top Brazilians Neymar ok.\n- brazilian_club_summary: Flamengo/Palmeiras/Corinthians/São Paulo have no players in the FIFA dataset; Santos 20, etc. But summary filter `players >= 1` and expects \"Flamengo\" in names — change to \"Santos\". Also BRAZILIAN_CLUBS list includes clubs not present — they're filtered out. Keep.\n\nAlso test_find_matches_between_two_teams asserted >5 for Fla-Flu — should be fine.\n\nAlso test \"all comps\" assertion: `any(c.startswith(\"Copa do Brasil\"))` fine; \"2003-2019\" fine.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05d947df9001nm7P2kXneeX39c","sessionID":"ses_fa26fadadffe2UVfX81vYXdx41","messageID":"msg_05d945e28001s7461Rgk4ys74U"}}
