is match between team A and B\": use keysets.\n\nSimplest: in analysis, replace normalize_team usage with:\n- `_keys(name)` from loader team_keys\n- team filter: `query_keys.isdisjoint(team_keys(m.home))` etc. — wait must consider alias match.\n\nPlan concretely. loader:\n\n```python\n_STATE_RE = re.compile(r\"[-–]\\s*([A-Z]{2})$\")\n\nALIASES = {\n    \"atletico mineiro\": {\"atletico mg\"},\n    \"atletico paranaense\": {\"atletico pr\"},\n    \"athletico paranaense\": {\"atletico pr\"},\n    \"atletico goianiense\": {\"atletico go\"},\n    \"america mineiro\": {\"america mg\"},\n    \"vasco\": {\"vasco gama\"},\n    \"sport recife\": {\"sport\"},\n    \"corinthians paulista\": {\"corinthians\"},\n}\n\ndef _clean(name):\n    name = (name or \"\").strip()\n    name = re.sub(r\"\\(.*?\\)\", \" \", name)\n    return strip_accents(name).lower()\n\ndef base_tokens(name):\n    toks = [t for t in re.split(r\"[^a-z0-9]+\", _clean(name)) if t]\n    state = \"\"\n    if len(toks) >= 2 and re.fullmatch(r\"[a-z]{2}\", toks[-1]) and toks[-1].upper() in STATES:\n        state = toks[-1]\n        toks = toks[:-1]\n    meaningful = [t for t in toks if t not in _NOISE_WORDS or ...keep]\n    if not meaningful: meaningful = toks\n    return meaningful, state\n```\n\nHmm wait, state detection: names like \"Avai-SC\" → tokens [\"avai\",\"sc\"] — \"sc\" is also a noise word (\"Sport Club\")! With STATES set containing \"sc\" as valid state abbreviation... \"Ceara Sporting Club\" → tokens [...,\"club\"]... \"SC\" as final token could be state Santa Catarina or Sport Club. Ambiguous. But \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\" ends with \"paulista\". OK, treat final 2-letter token that's a valid Brazilian UF as state: SC, MG, PR, GO, RJ, SP, RS, PE, CE, BA, AL, MT, MS, DF, PA, etc. Acceptable.\n\nBUT \"America-MG\" vs FIFA \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\": fine.\n\nAlso there's risk: \"Sport-PE\" → base \"sport\", state \"pe\" → key \"sport pe\". Query \"Sport Recife\" → alias \"sport\". Hmm al