sect team_keys(m.home).\n\nImplement:\n```python\ndef keys_of(name) -> frozenset\ndef match_key(name) -> str\n```\n\nanalysis changes: replace normalize_team with a small helper using keys_of:\n\n```python\ndef _team_filter(name): return keys_of(name)\nmatches_team = keys_of(x) & keys_of(y)\n```\n\nUpdate:\n- find_matches: team_keys_set = keys_of(team); membership: `team_keys_set & keys_of(m.home)` etc.\n- _record: compare via keys_of(m.home) & team_keys_set.\n- team_stats: use same.\n- head_to_head: set equality {keysA,keysB} — check (A&home and B&away) or (A&away and B&home).\n- standings: group by match_key(m.home).\n- search_players: club containment — use keys_of overlap or substring; keep substring on normalize... use keys_of(club) & keys_of(p.club)? FIFA \"Grêmio\" vs query \"Gremio\" fine. Use intersection, plus fallback substring. I'll use: club_key in keys or any key substring. Keep simple: intersection OR containment of base strings.\n\nLet me just use intersection for club.\n\n- players_at_club in SoccerData: index by keys_of(p.club).\n\nAlso \"se\" noise word (SE Palmeiras). Add \"se\", \"sociedade\", \"esportiva\" to noise. But careful \"se\" as standalone token only.\n\nAlso test expects normalize_team(\"SE Palmeiras\") == normalize_team(\"Palmeiras\") — keep normalize_team as base computation; tests use it. I'll keep public normalize_team returning base keyset string? The test asserts equality of strings. I'll make normalize_team return the base string (representative via group if applicable). \"SE Palmeiras\" → base \"palmeiras\" ✓. \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\" → tokens minus noise → \"corinthians paulista\"... hmm test expects == normalize_team(\"Corinthians\") = \"corinthians\". Add alias group {\"corinthians\",\"corinthians paulista\"} and normalize_team returns group representative. Good.\n\nresolve_team with keys.\n\nRewrite loader and analysis now. Also keep normalize_team exported for tests.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_