". My earlier ALIAS_GROUPS has \"corinthians paulista\" but the computed base is \"sport corinthians paulista\" (since sport is kept via _KEEP_IF_ALONE). Should \"sport\" be dropped when not alone? The rule: keep \"sport\" only if it's the ONLY token (team named just \"Sport\"). Fix filter: drop noise word if result non-empty; keep only if everything would be empty. So:\n\nmeaningful = [t for t in tokens if t not in _NOISE_WORDS] or tokens\n\nThat drops \"sport\" from \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\" → \"corinthians paulista\" → alias → \"corinthians\" ✓. And \"Sport\" alone → tokens [\"sport\"] → all dropped → fallback to tokens → \"sport\" ✓. And \"Sport-PE\" → base \"sport\" ✓ (state stripped, single token kept). But \"Sport Recife\" → \"recife\"! That breaks alias \"sport recife\"... \"Sport Recife\" → base \"recife\" — bad. Hmm. But FIFA club \"Sport Club do Recife\" → also \"recife\".\n\nAlternative: add alias {\"corinthians\", \"corinthians paulista\", \"sport corinthians paulista\"} and keep _KEEP_IF_ALONE rule. Then \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\" base = \"sport corinthians paulista\" → alias → matches \"corinthians\". ✓. And \"Sport Recife\" → \"sport recife\" → alias → {\"sport\"} ✓.\n\nSimpler: keep current filter, add \"sport corinthians paulista\" to the corinthians alias group. Also add \"sao paulo fc\"? base of \"São Paulo FC\" → tokens [sao, paulo, fc] → drop fc → \"sao paulo\" ✓ fine already.\n\nAlso test: normalize_team(\"Flamengo-RJ\")==normalize_team(\"Flamengo\") ✓.\n\nAlso fix \"palmeiras\" vs test expects equality only — fine.\n\nUpdate alias group. Also note test uses normalize_team — keep exported.\n\nAlso update tests/test_player... leftover Flamengo assertions in players_at_club (replace failed partially). Let me check the current test file for remaining \"Flamengo\" in players test.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05d97c1260017KxpBqc3o0q69S","sessionID":"ses_fa26fadadffe2UVfX81vYXdx41","messageID":"msg_05d979624001DW3K